<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh taka eases against dollar at opening.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh taka eases against dollar at opening.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bangladesh taka opened slightly weaker at 43.7500/7600 to the dollar in interbank trading on Monday against previous close at 43.7500/7520, dealers said.</p>
<p>The local unit would remain under pressure as importers' demand for the dollar was expected to be strong, dealers said.</p>
<p>The interbank call money rates opened at eight to 10 percent against previous at nine to 11 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Dhaka Newsroom +880-2-506363</p>
